# Senvoryn OS — CODEOWNERS
#
# Ownership expresses *who must review*, not *who decides*. Per GOVERNANCE.md
# §6.5, security-critical changes require at least two qualified reviewers,
# one of whom did not author the change. A single owner can never satisfy that
# requirement on their own — the second reviewer must come from outside the
# change's authorship.
#
# When the project grows past one steward, replace @johalputt with a team
# handle (for example @senvoryn/security) so that no individual becomes a
# single point of failure for release approval.

# Default reviewers
*                               @johalputt

# --- Security-critical paths: two qualified reviewers, one non-author -------
# Match the "security-critical" definition in CONTRIBUTING.md:
# capability enforcement, SCP gates, update verifier, installer, key handling,
# audit, privilege boundaries.
